@begin(section)

@title(Changelog)

All notable changes to zick are documented in this section.  The canonical,
up-to-date changelog lives in the repository's @c(CHANGELOG.md).

@begin(section)
@title(0.3.0 — 2026-08-14)

Added:

@begin(list)
@item(@c(zick verify --all) verifies every installed package in one
invocation, aggregates failures by package, and preserves exit code 4 for
any failure.)
@end(list)

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(0.2.0 — 2026-08-14)

Added:

@begin(list)
@item(Declarative project dependency workflows: @c(zick freeze) writes a
stable versioned @c(zick.lock.nrdl), and @c(zick sync) installs its packages
in dependency order with drift detection and @c(--dry-run) support.)
@item(@c(zick list) subcommand: prints every installed package with its
version, sorted by name.  An empty database prints nothing and exits 0.)
@item(@c(zick orphans) subcommand: lists the installed packages that nothing
depends on (the source nodes of the dependency graph).  Installing a package
that depends on another and then removing the depender leaves the dependency
reported by @c(orphans).)
@item(Project scaffolding: ASDF system @c(com.djhaskin.zick) with a tests
system, CLIFF-based entry point, Roswell script, Makefile, and ocicl
dependency pinning.)
@end(list)

Fixed:

@begin(list)
@item(NRDL output: command results that carry a collection (files,
dependers, dependees, removed packages, packages, orphans, verification
results) now emit FSet seqs, so an empty collection renders as @c([])
instead of @c(false), since NRDL maps nil, the empty CL list, to false.  Notably,
@c(zick orphans) on a store with no orphans previously printed
@c(orphaned-packages false).)
@item(@c(zick add -m) JSON metadata: NRDL reads JSON object keys back as
case-preserved keywords (e.g. @c(:|zick|)), which the metadata
keywordization skipped, so config-file/ghost-file classification (and
therefore upgrade put-aside/do-nothing decisions) was silently disabled for
packages installed with @c(-m).  Keys are now normalized to the store's
uppercase keywords (@c(:zick)/@c(:config-files)).)
@item(Smoke tests for the CLI entry point.)
@item(Port of @c(zic.fs): archive handling via zippy, SHA-256/CRC-32 via
ironclad, downloads via dexador/quri, and @c(.zick-db) marking-file search,
with a Parachute test suite (60 assertions).)
@item(Port of @c(zic.db): the package/file store as FSet persistent records
(@c(package-record)/@c(file)/@c(store)) serialized to a single NRDL document
via @c(slurp-store)/@c(save-store) — atomic temp + rename — with the full
query and mutation API (package-id, package-info, package-files, owned-by-p,
dependers/dependees, add-package, insert-file/use, remove-package/files/uses)
and a Parachute test suite (82 assertions).)
@item(Port of @c(zic.session): @c(with-zick-session) locks first, then opens
the database; @c(with-database) slurps/saves the NRDL store at
@c(.zick-db/packages.nrdl); @c(with-filelock) uses a lock file whose
existence is the lock, created atomically and removed on close, with zic's
descriptive error text adapted to zick; and @c(path-to-connection-string),
with a
Parachute test suite (18 assertions) including a cross-process
lock-contention test.)
@item(Black-box test environment: a python3 HTTPS fixture server with a
self-signed certificate (optional basic auth, user @c(mode) password
@c(code)) serving a wwwroot of @c(a.zip)/@c(b.zip)/@c(c.zip)/@c(bad.zip)
(the last with a corrupted entry for CRC-violation testing), plus
dsolv-style POSIX shell scripts (@c(tests/resources/scripts/test-*))
covering init/add/info/files/verify (exit codes 0/3/4)/remove/
dependers/dependees, run by @c(make test-black-box).)
@item(@c(zick remove) refusal now names the packages that depend on the one
being removed, and the dry-run path (@c(-r)/@c(--enable-dry-run)) is
exercised end to end: it reports the full removal set (dependers first under
@c(-c)) while leaving the package record, its files, and its config-file
backups untouched.)
@item(Install-next-to-existing-packages: @c(zick add) refuses an archive
whose files are already owned by another package, listing each clashing file
with its owner; disjoint installs succeed and both packages are queryable.
New @c(package-installable-p) and @c(list-archive-files) helpers back the
refusal.)
@item(Install-story test gaps closed: an instrumented test pins the HTTP
options @c(fs:download) sends for basic/header/oauth-token authorizations and
the insecure flag (by recording dexador:get's arguments); the store
serialization round-trip now also asserts package metadata and file classes
survive NRDL save/load; and the black-box @c(test-add) verifies the recorded
package end to end via @c(info) and @c(files) on a fresh database.)
@item(CLI download authorizations: @c(zick add) accepts
@c(--json-download-authorizations) — per-host @c(basic)/@c(header)/
@c(oauth-token) records, parsed with NRDL into @c(fs:download)'s auth table —
and @c(-n)/@c(--enable-insecure) reaches the HTTP client for self-signed
fixtures.  CLI subcommand functions renamed to standard Common Lisp names
(@c(add-command), @c(files-command), ...; no @c(!) suffix), per the style
guide.)
@item(Port of @c(zic.package): install/remove/verify of packages against the
NRDL store, with config-file upgrade precautions (install/put-aside/
do-nothing fates and in-place and downgrade guards via svers' debian-vercmp),
zip-based installs via zippy, dependency-aware removal (cascade vs refuse,
dry-run, sink-first linearization), file-conflict and checksum verification,
and the package query API, with a Parachute test suite (71 assertions).)
@item(Port of @c(zic.cli), from @c(src/main.lisp): the @c(zick) command line via
CLIFF with subcommands @c(add), @c(files), @c(info), @c(init), @c(remove),
@c(dependers), @c(dependees), and @c(verify) — plus @c(list) and
@c(orphans) — the zic short aliases, NRDL output, verify exit codes 3
(package not found) and 4 (verification failures), JSON package metadata for
@c(-m) parsed with NRDL, and the deprecated @c(.zic-db) marking-file fallback
(with a warning); @c(cl-json) dropped in favor of NRDL's JSON superset
parsing, with a CLI integration test suite (25 assertions).)
@end(list)

Changed:

@begin(list)
@item(Default output format is NRDL (zic's yaml default is dropped).)
@end(list)

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(0.1.0 — 2026-08-12)

Added:

@begin(list)
@item(Beads roadmap for porting zic to Common Lisp (20 issues), including the
database backend ADR and the ocicl library availability spike.)
@end(list)

@end(section)

@end(section)
